config BR2_PACKAGE_TOON_M4
	bool "toon-m4"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_ARM_GNU_TOOLCHAIN_SUPPORTS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_TOON_BUS
	help
	  Toon 2 Cortex-M4 sensor co-processor support: the M4 firmware
	  (ultrasonic wake-on-approach + VOC air-quality), loaded at boot
	  by the kernel's remoteproc (or m4load), and toon-m4d, which polls
	  the M4's shared mailbox and publishes the VOC index
	  (retoon/voc, toon-vocd-compatible) and motion/wake state
	  (retoon/motion) on the Toon's own MQTT broker.

	  The firmware is built from src/firmware with ARM's arm-none-eabi
	  toolchain (Buildroot host package arm-gnu-toolchain).

	  The ultrasonic detector needs gapless sampling, which only the
	  dedicated M4 core provides; the VOC gets PWM-phase-aligned ADC
	  samples the same way. Replaces toon-voc (do not enable both).

comment "toon-m4 needs an x86_64 or aarch64 build host"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_ARM_GNU_TOOLCHAIN_SUPPORTS
